WEBVTT

00:07.782 --> 00:13.542
Let's laugh and cry.
chanto waraimasho, nakimasho

00:14.142 --> 00:19.732
Subs originally by Froth-Bite
Manually retyped by #Retrofit@IRC.Rizon.Net
Raws by Darkside-Raws
We need to fill up our hearts.
kokoro no nakami wo juujitsu sasenakuccha

00:19.772 --> 00:28.322
Making matching memories with you...
anata to osoroi no omoide tsukuruno ga

00:28.322 --> 00:30.192
...is important.
daiji daiji

00:31.472 --> 00:34.022
Sometimes I become...
sunao ni narenakattari

00:34.352 --> 00:37.852
...almost dishonest and mean
ijiwaru shichaisouna hi aruno

00:39.352 --> 00:40.692
That's because...
sore wa...

00:42.692 --> 00:45.442
I love you and adore you,
daisuki de taisetsu de

00:45.572 --> 00:48.782
and I don't want to be apart from you.
hanaretaku nai sei nano nante

00:50.742 --> 00:51.742
That's the truth.
henne

00:54.292 --> 01:01.002
I just want to cuddle...
hontou wa itsumo nuku nuku shitetai

01:01.332 --> 01:03.342
...with you.
futaride

01:04.342 --> 01:10.052
So let's laugh and cry.
dakara waraimashou, nakimashou

01:10.722 --> 01:16.142
We need to keep our hearts warm.
kokoro no ondo wo atatame awanakucha

01:16.352 --> 01:24.782
The fate that made us meet...
anata to deaeta unmei ho subetega

01:24.782 --> 01:26.482
...is important.
daiji daiji

01:41.472 --> 01:42.932
It's a beautiful day!

01:42.932 --> 01:44.182
It's a perfect...

01:44.182 --> 01:46.442
...day for a picnic!

01:46.942 --> 01:48.522
Yes!

01:54.692 --> 01:56.782
It really is a great day.

01:57.702 --> 01:59.612
Let's have fun, Mom.

02:00.832 --> 02:02.412
Are you okay, Mom?

02:02.912 --> 02:05.912
So, Momono-san, what's in here?

02:06.372 --> 02:09.922
You'll find out once we get there.

02:09.922 --> 02:11.632
Thanks.

02:11.632 --> 02:13.172
Y-yes...

02:17.972 --> 02:19.932
Come on, Mom.

02:20.472 --> 02:23.762
It will be so tough without these boxes this month.

02:25.142 --> 02:27.932
What exactly are they going to use those cardboard boxes for?

02:37.612 --> 02:39.242
A red maple leaf-viewing picnic...

02:42.662 --> 02:43.952
Shiratori-san.

02:43.952 --> 02:45.442
Hurry!

02:45.442 --> 02:46.952
Oh, I'm coming.

02:50.292 --> 02:51.122
Oh?

02:54.712 --> 02:56.342
It's really heavy.

02:56.342 --> 02:57.632
What's in it anyway?

03:09.982 --> 03:11.392
Are you okay?

03:15.152 --> 03:16.362
Kozue-chan...

03:21.572 --> 03:23.322
Let's hurry ahead!

03:24.832 --> 03:26.492
K-Kozue-chan...

03:31.832 --> 03:36.552
Among the Red Leaves

03:36.552 --> 03:38.962
We are using the train today?
Among the Red Leaves

03:38.962 --> 03:38.972
Among the Red Leaves

03:38.972 --> 03:39.712
Are we going far?
Among the Red Leaves

03:40.172 --> 03:43.012
No, the place that we're going is only five stations away,

03:43.012 --> 03:44.512
so it's not that far from here.

03:47.772 --> 03:49.932
Here you go.

03:49.932 --> 03:50.642
Yes.

03:50.642 --> 03:51.942
Don't lose them.

03:51.942 --> 03:52.602
Thank you.

03:53.442 --> 03:54.102
Bite.

03:54.812 --> 03:56.062
Especially you, Shiratori-kun!

03:56.072 --> 03:56.902
Yes?

03:57.362 --> 03:59.942
You are the most undependable.

04:05.122 --> 04:08.122
Just as I thought, you got the bad ticket!

04:08.122 --> 04:08.952
Momono-san?

04:09.292 --> 04:10.872
The bad ticket?

04:12.332 --> 04:16.042
I had one fake ticket in the mix.

04:20.842 --> 04:22.132
C-crap!

04:22.132 --> 04:22.922
The train is leaving!

04:23.222 --> 04:25.012
Let's run for it everyone!

04:28.392 --> 04:30.142
The doors are closing now.

04:30.142 --> 04:31.142
Please be careful.

04:37.312 --> 04:37.982
Yeah!

04:38.322 --> 04:40.112
We just made it.

04:40.112 --> 04:42.652
We didn't have to rush.

04:42.652 --> 04:45.492
We could have taken the next train.

04:45.872 --> 04:47.072
Tsk, tsk, tsk.

04:47.072 --> 04:48.582
Life is short.

04:48.582 --> 04:50.992
We must not waste even one second of it.

04:57.212 --> 04:59.962
Traveling on a train is all right, every now and then.

05:03.722 --> 05:04.632
Asami-chan!

05:04.632 --> 05:05.552
Sayo-chan!

05:08.142 --> 05:09.432
Everyone...

05:23.902 --> 05:28.532
So running for that train was meaningless after all, since we ended up waiting for the next train anyway.

05:28.782 --> 05:30.452
It's all well and good.

05:30.452 --> 05:34.002
This is how we make enjoyable memories.

05:35.032 --> 05:36.462
Well,

05:36.462 --> 05:37.542
that's true.

05:38.882 --> 05:40.342
Looks like it's here.

05:40.882 --> 05:42.052
Finally.

05:57.232 --> 05:59.522
Oh, that's strange.

05:59.522 --> 06:01.652
They aren't on that one?

06:01.652 --> 06:04.072
Maybe they're on the next one...

06:08.912 --> 06:10.702
They were on that one.

06:10.702 --> 06:13.582
And that's yet another enjoyable memory.

06:26.552 --> 06:27.672
Now, now,

06:27.682 --> 06:31.092
we've already done a lot, but here comes today's main event!

06:34.182 --> 06:37.062
This is our site for viewing the red maple leaves!

06:38.392 --> 06:41.392
Omori Park

07:04.712 --> 07:06.212
It's gorgeous.

07:06.842 --> 07:07.922
Yes, it is.

07:08.222 --> 07:10.552
Look, look, there's a pond!

07:13.602 --> 07:15.762
Are there fish in it?

07:16.772 --> 07:17.722
I don't know.

07:17.732 --> 07:19.772
It's a man-made pond, so I don't think so...

07:25.402 --> 07:26.502
Asami-chan?

07:35.702 --> 07:36.952
I know.

07:37.582 --> 07:39.702
That money was not lost.

07:40.122 --> 07:44.292
That money was thrown in there, filled with people's wishes.

07:45.502 --> 07:47.002
I know.

07:47.002 --> 07:48.382
I know, but...

07:48.382 --> 07:49.712
I know...

07:49.722 --> 07:50.842
I know, but...

07:54.052 --> 07:56.302
Asami, look.

07:56.312 --> 07:57.642
Um, that's...

08:08.732 --> 08:09.482
<i>What?</i>

08:09.492 --> 08:11.652
<i>What kind of face did she make?</i>

08:14.362 --> 08:18.082
It feels so different from Narutakisou's courtyard here.

08:18.082 --> 08:19.122
It feels so great here!

08:19.452 --> 08:20.952
I know.

08:20.952 --> 08:24.212
The landscape is so vast, and the air feels so good.

08:24.212 --> 08:27.382
I'm with you, so it's even better!

08:27.842 --> 08:32.262
Maybe it's because it's the peak of the season, but there are a lot of people here.

08:32.262 --> 08:34.802
Can we even find a spot for us to set up for our party?

08:37.392 --> 08:39.262
Private Johnny! Private Tamami!

08:39.262 --> 08:41.392
This is an emergency!

08:41.392 --> 08:43.182
What is it, Captain Momo?

08:43.982 --> 08:47.522
We must secure our base or else there will be no tomorrow!

08:47.522 --> 08:49.572
Do you understand what I mean?!

08:49.572 --> 08:52.032
Rogar that, Captain Momo.

08:52.652 --> 08:54.032
What is it?

08:54.032 --> 08:55.572
Private Shiratori!

08:55.952 --> 08:56.612
The package!

08:58.162 --> 08:59.082
Yes!

08:59.082 --> 08:59.872
Let's go!

08:59.872 --> 09:01.162
Charge!

09:01.502 --> 09:03.162
Yeah!

09:03.712 --> 09:06.122
Charge!

09:06.122 --> 09:07.332
Go!

09:17.762 --> 09:20.512
Isn't it pretty, Shiratori-san?

09:20.512 --> 09:21.182
Yeah.

09:21.602 --> 09:23.722
Should we go for a walk?

09:23.732 --> 09:25.272
Oh, sure.

09:25.272 --> 09:26.812
Hey!

09:27.692 --> 09:30.862
You guys hurry up too!

09:30.862 --> 09:32.072
Okay.

09:38.822 --> 09:41.202
The red maple leaf-viewing picnic can't start without this!

09:41.202 --> 09:43.042
Wow! I've been waiting for it!

09:48.292 --> 09:50.132
No wonder it was so heavy.

09:50.132 --> 09:50.882
Here.

09:52.002 --> 09:53.592
But it's not a cherry blossom festival.

09:53.592 --> 09:55.462
Please don't.

09:55.472 --> 09:56.922
I can't!

09:56.932 --> 09:59.052
Don't be so rigid.

09:59.052 --> 10:00.642
Come on, under-age boy.

10:00.642 --> 10:02.892
Only as a gesture, then.

10:02.892 --> 10:05.982
Hey, can I have something to snack on?

10:05.982 --> 10:07.392
I'm hungry.

10:07.392 --> 10:11.112
Captain Momo, where is lunch?

10:11.112 --> 10:13.902
Don't we have any food?

10:14.532 --> 10:18.492
It looks like this container only has drinks in it.

10:18.862 --> 10:23.412
Please don't tell me that we only brought drinks.

10:25.662 --> 10:26.752
Yes, sir!

10:31.172 --> 10:33.292
It's okay, everyone.

10:33.302 --> 10:36.632
I brought all the lunch and snacks we need.

10:36.972 --> 10:38.132
Kozue-chan!

10:39.012 --> 10:40.182
That's great.

10:45.722 --> 10:47.772
Eat a lot.

10:48.692 --> 10:50.192
Yay!

10:50.192 --> 10:53.022
Let's eat!

11:07.912 --> 11:08.412
Next one!

11:08.412 --> 11:09.752
Here I go!

11:19.132 --> 11:21.472
Captain, that's great.

11:21.472 --> 11:25.642
In this damn cold weather, you are drinking this super cold beer.

11:25.642 --> 11:28.062
And that was your twenty-first can.

11:28.852 --> 11:29.432
Time for the next one!

11:29.432 --> 11:31.062
Here I go!

11:31.732 --> 11:32.942
Yay!

11:42.532 --> 11:44.282
So sour!

11:47.082 --> 11:48.702
So sour!

11:49.332 --> 11:50.292
Is it umeboshi?

11:50.872 --> 11:53.042
Yes, it is.

11:55.462 --> 11:57.382
This smells like...

11:58.992 --> 12:00.592
What's wrong?

12:02.342 --> 12:02.972
Don't tell me...

12:06.182 --> 12:08.512
Onii-chan, we found a lot!

12:09.522 --> 12:10.472
Of what?

12:11.282 --> 12:12.252
Ta-daa!

12:12.252 --> 12:13.472
Gingko Nuts
Ta-daa!

12:13.472 --> 12:14.002
Gingko Nuts

12:14.022 --> 12:16.062
G-ginko nuts?

12:16.062 --> 12:18.072
I knew it.

12:19.072 --> 12:22.112
We will survive on roasted gingko nuts this month.

12:22.112 --> 12:25.072
Let's share some with Mahiru-chan, Mom.

12:26.452 --> 12:29.082
So, Sayoko-san, your box is also...

12:32.372 --> 12:33.832
Ta-daa!

12:33.832 --> 12:35.122
Acorns
Ta-daa!

12:35.122 --> 12:35.582
Acorns

12:36.002 --> 12:38.212
Um, Sayoko-san,

12:40.592 --> 12:42.762
you can't eat acorns.

12:50.812 --> 12:53.102
Man, I drank a lot!

12:53.102 --> 12:56.232
Captain, you just broke your record.

12:56.232 --> 13:00.112
It's also amazing that you never went to the bathroom the whole time.

13:00.482 --> 13:01.192
Of course.

13:01.192 --> 13:02.612
I'm the captain.

13:04.072 --> 13:06.822
You drank too much.

13:06.822 --> 13:08.452
What are you talking about?

13:08.452 --> 13:11.122
Why do you think I drank so fast?

13:18.632 --> 13:22.712
You drank for me, so that the luggage would be lighter?!

13:22.712 --> 13:24.172
No!

13:24.172 --> 13:25.802
To put these in it!

13:27.142 --> 13:28.932
Thank you, Onii-chan!

13:29.052 --> 13:31.432
Thank you, Onii-chan!

13:31.432 --> 13:33.102
Oh, you're welc...

13:33.102 --> 13:34.522
Onii-chan?

13:35.062 --> 13:37.982
Now that we're full,

13:37.982 --> 13:41.942
let's play tag, as usual!

13:41.942 --> 13:43.982
Yay!

13:43.992 --> 13:47.452
And I'm it, as usual, right?

13:47.992 --> 13:48.952
Of course.

14:01.422 --> 14:04.552
They ran away so fast.

14:05.342 --> 14:08.432
I won't catch up to any of them at this rate.

14:23.112 --> 14:24.612
Nobody is coming.

14:24.612 --> 14:26.742
I need to go out...

14:33.122 --> 14:34.542
Somebody came after all.

14:34.542 --> 14:35.702
Good...

14:38.002 --> 14:39.462
There you are!

14:39.792 --> 14:42.462
I caught...

14:42.752 --> 14:43.462
...you...

14:46.802 --> 14:48.762
K-Kozue-chan...

14:50.972 --> 14:52.932
I got caught.

15:03.612 --> 15:07.862
They will get away very easily even if I do spot them...

15:07.862 --> 15:09.322
It's okay.

15:10.032 --> 15:13.372
I will run fast so that I won't be a burden.

15:14.532 --> 15:16.032
Let's catch them.

15:21.002 --> 15:22.622
Are you okay, Kozue-chan?

15:23.332 --> 15:24.462
Oh, yes.

15:25.632 --> 15:30.382
You might have gotten a little cold from all the sweating you did by running so much.

15:30.932 --> 15:32.592
Oh, yeah!

15:32.592 --> 15:34.092
This way!

15:34.102 --> 15:35.642
Shiratori-san?

15:42.652 --> 15:44.352
It's so warm.

15:49.192 --> 15:50.322
Good.

15:55.702 --> 15:56.622
Huh?!

15:56.622 --> 15:57.412
Tamami-chan?!

15:58.952 --> 16:00.912
I got caught.

16:01.792 --> 16:03.872
Isn't it warm?

16:08.502 --> 16:10.762
Gotcha!

16:14.682 --> 16:15.512
I broke you free!

16:15.512 --> 16:17.552
Run away now!

16:18.602 --> 16:21.142
I thought this was chain tag!

16:21.562 --> 16:23.812
It's Narutakisou's house rules!

16:23.812 --> 16:25.852
Breaking the chain frees everyone!

16:33.322 --> 16:35.412
I'm so glad, Kozue-chan.

16:35.412 --> 16:36.782
Now we are...

16:37.782 --> 16:40.492
Oh, no!

16:45.422 --> 16:46.752
What are you doing?!

16:46.752 --> 16:48.752
I got caught again.

16:49.712 --> 16:51.002
Go!

16:57.682 --> 16:59.512
Are you okay, Kozue-chan?

17:00.522 --> 17:03.102
I got caught again.

17:06.402 --> 17:08.652
So that's how you play...

18:05.912 --> 18:08.962
Man, I'm beat!

18:09.422 --> 18:11.542
But we had fun.

18:11.542 --> 18:13.212
Yes.

18:13.212 --> 18:15.382
Asami, dinner...

18:15.382 --> 18:17.632
Let's roast some gingko nuts when we get home.

18:17.632 --> 18:19.892
Acorn rice...

18:19.892 --> 18:22.642
Let's pack up and start heading home.

18:22.642 --> 18:25.272
I second that.

18:43.992 --> 18:46.582
Everyone fell asleep.

18:46.582 --> 18:47.122
Yes.

18:47.752 --> 18:49.962
We played so hard.

18:49.962 --> 18:51.712
No wonder everyone got tired.

18:54.342 --> 18:56.302
Are you okay, Shiratori-san?

18:56.762 --> 18:58.552
Of course I am.

19:00.512 --> 19:02.222
Or maybe not?

19:04.102 --> 19:07.392
The days since you arrived have been filled with delight.

19:08.602 --> 19:09.732
Since I arrived?

19:09.732 --> 19:10.562
Yes.

19:12.732 --> 19:15.272
Weren't the red leaves pretty?

19:16.112 --> 19:17.402
Yeah.

19:17.402 --> 19:22.572
I feel really fortunate to be born in a country with such beautiful seasons when I see such scenes.

19:22.572 --> 19:24.072
Me too.

19:25.032 --> 19:26.872
We have cherry blossom festivals in the spring,

19:27.582 --> 19:29.832
the beach in the summer,

19:30.412 --> 19:32.712
and in the fall, we can go see the leaves turn red.

19:33.882 --> 19:35.422
We even played hide and seek,

19:35.422 --> 19:38.052
and visited the local school festival too.

19:38.712 --> 19:41.092
I wonder what we'll do next?

19:41.092 --> 19:44.552
Maybe we'll have a snowball fight in the winter?

19:46.392 --> 19:47.352
Kozue-chan?

19:49.772 --> 19:52.232
I wonder how many more...

19:54.652 --> 19:59.822
I wonder how many more times we'll be able to spend the seasons together.

20:00.782 --> 20:02.032
Kozue-chan...

20:03.112 --> 20:05.242
I'm sure many, many more!

20:05.242 --> 20:09.992
We'll go to many places and do many things together, won't we?

20:10.622 --> 20:15.922
But everyone will eventually leave Narutakisou, right?

20:19.132 --> 20:21.262
Right, Shiratori-san?

20:30.892 --> 20:32.482
It's okay, Shiratori-san.

20:33.352 --> 20:34.232
No.

20:36.942 --> 20:38.152
Kozue-chan,

20:39.192 --> 20:42.152
from here on, let's keep creating more memories...

20:44.282 --> 20:45.202
...for...

20:45.782 --> 20:47.202
...for all eternity, together.

20:50.332 --> 20:51.832
Shiratori-san...

20:56.292 --> 20:58.792
I mean...

20:59.842 --> 21:00.752
Sure!

21:06.342 --> 21:07.892
By the way, Kozue-chan.

21:07.892 --> 21:08.302
Yes?

21:08.302 --> 21:10.762
So, for dinner tonight...

21:10.762 --> 21:13.312
...should we ask them to share a few of their gingko nuts?

21:13.312 --> 21:14.482
Just as I thought.

